    "updated_at": "2021-09-27T05:03:03Z",
    "body": "Issue appears to be WezTerm is spawning bash as a login shell. So, when I log into a tty then open WezTerm, it's sourcing the bash configuration files twice. Or so I assume. Changing it to not spawn a login shell remove the job indicator.\r\n\r\nNot sure if that's still a bug on the `job` module, as my other shells (e.g. Zsh) were also being spawned as a login shell, but the job indicator was not shown for them.",
