    "updated_at": "2021-10-17T00:58:40Z",
    "body": "This also happens when using `jump` for fuzzy dir navigation.\r\n\r\nI suspect in that case it's because both starship and jump make use of pre/post exec functions in bash - jump scores the dir you are in after every command - it's possible that while starship is calculating jobs in bash that other precesses kicking off automatical get included but can't be seen after the prompt finished rendering.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
