    "body": "> I found out what the job is in my case:\r\n> \r\n> `wezterm set-working-directory 2> /dev/null`\r\n> [...]\r\n> Aw jeez.\r\n> \r\n> [The culprit is `__wezterm_osc_7` in the shell integration](https://github.com/wez/wezterm/blob/7deb215303ce1a8e64d48f65ef3e0a1d24fc2fbc/assets/shell-integration/wezterm.sh#L387), which attempts to set the title of the terminal using a `wezterm` command.\r\n\r\nWoah. How on earth did you debug this find? :sweat_smile: That's great!\r\n\r\n> Longer-term, I think those of us that try to write tooling for bash need to hash out some common framework to make these kinds of things work--bash-preexec is a good first step towards that direction, but I'm not convinced it's complete.\r\n\r\nI agree. TBH, this bug was annoying me so much that I switched to ZSH :see_no_evil: ",
