    "body": "> How did you debug this find?\r\n\r\nModifying the init scripts by dumping them into disk, along with a little bit of `set -x`. Basically used that to find out that the errant command was running wezterm, then looked into the wezterm codebase \r\n\r\n> I resolved it by not using a login shell.\r\n\r\nI don't entirely understand what this has to do with it still, though I found the same as you (that not using a login shell gets rid of it). How did you install WezTerm? When tracing my execution, I found a reference to `. /etc/profile.d/wezterm.sh` meaning that the wezterm integration scripts were run at a system level (meaning only for login shells).",
