    "body": "Yes, `set -x` causes bash to \"trace\" its execution by echoing every statement before it's executed. Doesn't always give you 100% of what you want, but it's pretty good. (BTW, also works in zsh!)\r\n\r\nAnd yes, it's probably wezterm in this case, but this is hardly restricted to it, since frameworks like autojump and z.sh have been known to cause similar issues. Still, maybe we should open an issue on their end to see if they have any ideas.",
