    "body": "👋🏻 just pinging to say that on macOS I see '2' jobs highlighted when there is only 1 job. If I just open up a fresh terminal then I'll immediately see the icon for the jobs module to suggest 1 job is running (when there isn't).\r\n\r\nI'm not sure why this is but then I stumbled onto this issue which suggests it's because (although I'm using the Alacritty terminal) it's to do with how macOS handles new terminal windows (i.e. macOS will start a 'login' shell which means `.bash_profile` is sourced but not `.bashrc`, and so I have to explicitly source my `.bashrc` from the `.bash_profile` otherwise it won't be loaded).",
