    "updated_at": "2024-04-01T08:33:44Z",
    "body": "I think this was fixed by #5253, though I haven't tested it with Wezterm. This is caused by the behavior of Bash 5.1 where `jobs` reports also the foreground dead jobs created in `PROMPT_COMMAND`. The `printf` command doesn't create a foreground job because it's a builtin command, while the `wezterm` command creates a foreground job and leaves a job entry in `PROMPT_COMMAND`.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
